From: turbinebmw <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 10:35:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100: drop QCE sleep bandwidth
 vote

The QCE driver installs a constant 393600 kB/s memory interconnect vote at probe time. The X1E80100 device tree tags that path for active, wake and sleep buckets, so the vote remains in the RPMh sleep batch after QCE and the rest of the devices have suspended.

QCE cannot issue transactions after APSS enters suspend. Tag its memory path active-only so the normal and wake constraints are preserved while the sleep bucket can fall to zero.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
index cd462c6231ff476d18704b2d5389e1c4ed8b47f5..8ec65b489ea367ffcf8e6b37a8e92500a7ead2c7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
@@ -4027,8 +4027,8 @@ crypto: crypto@1dfa000 {
 				    "tx";
 			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x480 0x0>,
 				 <&apps_smmu 0x481 0x0>;
-			interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_CRYPTO QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
-					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
+			interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_CRYPTO QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY
+					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>;
 			interconnect-names = "memory";
 		};
 
